The function classifies triangles defined by each set of three consecutive vertices by the sign of the cross product of the two form vectors from a shared vertex. A positive value means a counter-clockwise turn about the shared vertex, a negative value means a clockwise turn, and a value near zero comes from near-collinear points. For an otherwise collinear polygon such as a straight line every sign is zero, so the function returns False for that corner case. The iteration wraps around the ends of the list with modulo arithmetic, and the result is True only when the polygon consistently turns in the same direction everywhere.

