A pedestrian arriving on a tick the light already belongs to is placed at that tick only if that tick is red; if it is green, the code skips forward past that block and places the pedestrian at the start of the next red block. A pedestrian arriving after the end of the list is placed at the closest red tick after the arrival time. For each pedestrian the placement is computed with only one query of where the light is red. The code returns the crossing ticks in arrival order.

