An n-vertex polygon is convex exactly when every three consecutive vertices turn in the same direction, counter-clockwise in one convention and clockwise in the other, and no three vertices lie on a straight line. Because the example input of four points can only hold half a turn at the inside corner, the three-point input, a triangle, needs the collinearity check separately, but it is also required by the specification.

